        <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold leading-tight" style="color: var(--theme-text);">Standard-Parts Procurement FAQ</h2>
      </header>
      <div class="max-w-4xl space-y-3">
        <details class="group rounded-xl border p-5" style="background: var(--theme-bg); border-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--theme-primary) 14%, transparent);">
          <summary class="cursor-pointer flex items-start gap-3 list-none">
            <span class="shrink-0 w-7 h-7 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center text-xs font-bold" style="background: var(--theme-primary); color: var(--theme-text);">1</span>
            <h3 class="flex-1 text-base font-bold" style="color: var(--theme-text);">What titanium standard parts does BOZE supply?</h3>
          </summary>
          <p class="mt-3 ml-10 text-sm leading-relaxed">BOZE supplies catalog-spec titanium fasteners, flanges, pipe fittings and CNC-machined standard components. Typical families include slip-on / weld-neck / blind flanges per ASME B16.5, butt-weld and forged fittings per ASME B16.9 / B16.11, bolts / nuts / washers per ASTM F467 / DIN / ISO, and standard machined components such as spacers, sleeves, rings, bushings, pins and collars.</p>
        </details>

        <details class="group rounded-xl border p-5" style="background: var(--theme-bg); border-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--theme-primary) 14%, transparent);">
          <summary class="cursor-pointer flex items-start gap-3 list-none">
            <span class="shrink-0 w-7 h-7 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center text-xs font-bold" style="background: var(--theme-primary); color: var(--theme-text);">2</span>
            <h3 class="flex-1 text-base font-bold" style="color: var(--theme-text);">Which titanium grades are available?</h3>
          </summary>
          <p class="mt-3 ml-10 text-sm leading-relaxed">Commercially pure Grades 1 and 2, Grade 5 (Ti-6Al-4V), Grade 7 (Ti-0.15Pd), Grade 9 (Ti-3Al-2.5V), Grade 12 (Ti-0.3Mo-0.8Ni) and Grade 23 (Ti-6Al-4V ELI) are commonly specified. Specific grade availability depends on product form and applicable standard -- see the Grade x Standard matrix.</p>
        </details>

        <details class="group rounded-xl border p-5" style="background: var(--theme-bg); border-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--theme-primary) 14%, transparent);">
          <summary class="cursor-pointer flex items-start gap-3 list-none">
            <span class="shrink-0 w-7 h-7 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center text-xs font-bold" style="background: var(--theme-primary); color: var(--theme-text);">3</span>
            <h3 class="flex-1 text-base font-bold" style="color: var(--theme-text);">Which ASTM and ASME standards do your titanium parts follow?</h3>
          </summary>
          <p class="mt-3 ml-10 text-sm leading-relaxed">Commonly supplied to ASTM B348 (bars / billets), B381 (forgings -- flanges), B363 (wrought fittings), B338 (tubes), B265 (plate / sheet), B861 (seamless pipe), B862 (welded pipe), F467 (fasteners), F67 (medical CP-Ti), F136 (medical Ti-6Al-4V ELI) and to ASME B16.5 / B16.9 / B16.11 / B16.28.</p>
        </details>

        <details class="group rounded-xl border p-5" style="background: var(--theme-bg); border-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--theme-primary) 14%, transparent);">
          <summary class="cursor-pointer flex items-start gap-3 list-none">
            <span class="shrink-0 w-7 h-7 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center text-xs font-bold" style="background: var(--theme-primary); color: var(--theme-text);">4</span>
            <h3 class="flex-1 text-base font-bold" style="color: var(--theme-text);">Can you provide MTR or MTC documentation?</h3>
          </summary>
          <p class="mt-3 ml-10 text-sm leading-relaxed">Yes. EN 10204 Type 3.1 mill test certificates are available as standard documentation. 3.2 certificates (independent third-party validation) are accommodated on request. CoC, dimensional inspection report, FAIR and hydrostatic test report are available on a project-dependent basis (see the Documentation Package section).</p>
        </details>

        <details class="group rounded-xl border p-5" style="background: var(--theme-bg); border-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--theme-primary) 14%, transparent);">
          <summary class="cursor-pointer flex items-start gap-3 list-none">
            <span class="shrink-0 w-7 h-7 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center text-xs font-bold" style="background: var(--theme-primary); color: var(--theme-text);">5</span>
            <h3 class="flex-1 text-base font-bold" style="color: var(--theme-text);">Can titanium standard parts be CNC machined to modified dimensions?</h3>
          </summary>
          <p class="mt-3 ml-10 text-sm leading-relaxed">Yes. BOZE is not limited to catalog supply -- when a standard component requires modified dimensions, special tolerances, non-standard threads, additional machining features or drawing-specific geometry, our CNC manufacturing capability provides a direct path from standard specification to engineered component.</p>
        </details>

        <details class="group rounded-xl border p-5" style="background: var(--theme-bg); border-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--theme-primary) 14%, transparent);">
          <summary class="cursor-pointer flex items-start gap-3 list-none">
            <span class="shrink-0 w-7 h-7 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center text-xs font-bold" style="background: var(--theme-primary); color: var(--theme-text);">6</span>
            <h3 class="flex-1 text-base font-bold" style="color: var(--theme-text);">Can you supply titanium pipe fittings and flanges to ASME requirements?</h3>
          </summary>
          <p class="mt-3 ml-10 text-sm leading-relaxed">Yes. Butt-weld fittings per ASME B16.9 (and B16.28 for short-radius returns), forged fittings per ASME B16.11, and flanges per ASME B16.5 / B16.47 dimensional requirements. Material backing is typically ASTM B363 (wrought) or ASTM B381 (forged) per project specification.</p>
        </details>

        <details class="group rounded-xl border p-5" style="background: var(--theme-bg); border-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--theme-primary) 14%, transparent);">
          <summary class="cursor-pointer flex items-start gap-3 list-none">
            <span class="shrink-0 w-7 h-7 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center text-xs font-bold" style="background: var(--theme-primary); color: var(--theme-text);">7</span>
            <h3 class="flex-1 text-base font-bold" style="color: var(--theme-text);">Can BOZE provide material and heat-number traceability?</h3>
          </summary>
          <p class="mt-3 ml-10 text-sm leading-relaxed">Yes. Heat-to-part material traceability is available as a standard documentation output: the mill heat number is recorded at incoming inspection and persists through processing, dimensional inspection and shipment.</p>
        </details>

        <details class="group rounded-xl border p-5" style="background: var(--theme-bg); border-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--theme-primary) 14%, transparent);">
          <summary class="cursor-pointer flex items-start gap-3 list-none">
            <span class="shrink-0 w-7 h-7 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center text-xs font-bold" style="background: var(--theme-primary); color: var(--theme-text);">8</span>
            <h3 class="flex-1 text-base font-bold" style="color: var(--theme-text);">Can you manufacture a standard part from our drawing?</h3>
          </summary>
          <p class="mt-3 ml-10 text-sm leading-relaxed">Yes. When your requirement deviates from a catalog specification -- different dimensions, tighter tolerances, special threads, additional features or project-specific geometry -- submit your drawing with the applicable standard reference. Our engineering team reviews dimensional changes, material requirements and inspection requirements, then returns a quotation aligned to your drawing.</p>
        </details>
